## Signature

- Provided by: **Space Bunny Alpha (space-bunny-alpha)** — 2026-09-25
- Method: public internet research of modelbenchmark.io (Omen Alpha spec page and leaderboard), LLM Stats (Omen Alpha model page and Kimi K2.8 comparisons), the OpenCode Zen model catalog, and the Artificial Analysis LLM leaderboard. Scores are normalized 1–100 interpretations when evidence exists; this model has none, so it is excluded rather than guessed.
- Future sources: if any independent leaderboard publishes a score for `opencode-go/omen-alpha`, add a new file next to this one using the same headings and retire this twin.


- No verified public score found. Omen Alpha is **absent from the modelbenchmark.io leaderboard**, which ranks 82 models that have at least 3 benchmarks from at least 2 independent sources — so it has no qualifying evidence at all. No Terminal-Bench, τ-bench, Toolathon, MCP-Atlas, Claw-Eval or GDPval figure is published.

Reasoning / knowledge:

- No verified public score found — no GPQA Diamond, HLE, AIME, CritPt or Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index number exists. The model is not on the Artificial Analysis LLM leaderboard (172 models), and the LLM Stats page for it is a stub with no scores, no latency and no speed data.

Coding:

- No verified public score found — no SWE-bench Verified, LiveCodeBench, SciCode, DeepSWE or Vibe Code Bench figure is published for this model.

Long context:

- No long-context retrieval benchmark reported (no MRCR / RULER / GraphWalks row). The 500K window is a spec-sheet figure only; **no measured retrieval result at 512K+** is published, so a 100/100 context score would be unjustifiable even if text benchmarks existed.
- Throughput and latency: **not published** (LLM Stats shows "—" for speed and latency).
